  "tune": "public domain: traditional, printed 1914",
  "arrangement": "original, written for Stackapella on the harmony of Cecil Sharp's piano accompaniment (public domain: printed 1914, Sharp died 1924); the tune as printed, with breaths written in for beginners",
  "recordings": "synthesized guides",
  "checked": null,
  "source": "tune and words from Cecil J. Sharp, English Folk-Chanteys, with pianoforte accompaniment, introduction and notes (London: Simpkin, Marshall, Hamilton, Kent & Co. and Schott & Co.; Taunton: Barnicott & Pearce, the Wessex Press, 1914), No. II, \"Leave her Johnny\", first version, p. 3, with Sharp's note on p. 65 (\"First version sung by Mr. John Short, at Watchet\"), in E dorian as printed; verses 1 to 3 of his seven; the harmony of the chorus parts from his piano accompaniment. New York Public Library copy, read from the scan at archive.org/details/englishfolkchant00shar (p. 3 is leaf n23, the note leaf n85)"
